# Experiment 14, the third answer: an ore line built in the twentieth century.
#
# Extract, crush, move. The ore path is five components in a straight line and
# the power system is bolted underneath it, one motor per machine:
#
#   mains -> motor -> gearbox -> crusher
#
# There is no prime mover on site. There is no line shaft. Each crusher has its
# own motor two tiles below it, and the only reason the gearbox is there at all
# is that a motor turns at speed 6 and a crusher will not take more than 2.
#
# There is also no wiring in this file, and that is deliberate rather than an
# omission. A power connection reaches twenty-four tiles, so the grid connection
# in the corner feeds every motor in the plant directly. Running a cable between
# them was a question with one answer, and a question with one answer is not a
# design decision -- it is stationery. See `parts::REACH_POWER`.
#
# What this design does *not* contain is the interesting part:
#
#   no belt       steel rates 9 and a crusher shakes at 7, so nothing anywhere
#                 in this plant needs isolating from anything else
#   no cooling    a motor settles at 30 degrees and its range runs to 60
#   no water      nothing here is a heat engine
#   no spacing    the plot is tight on purpose, and nothing minds
#
# The cost is on one line of the scoreboard, and it is the only line: grid draw,
# metered, every tick.

machine "Electric Ore Line"
brief line

inlet     I1  at 0,0    draws ore

crusher   C1  at 4,0
crusher   C2  at 9,0
screw     SC1 at 14,0
outlet    O1  at 18,0

gearbox   GB1 at 5,4   ratio 4
gearbox   GB2 at 10,4  ratio 4
gearbox   GB3 at 15,4  ratio 2
motor     MO1 at 4,7
motor     MO2 at 9,7
motor     MO3 at 14,7
mains     M1  at 0,7

wire M1.power -> MO1.power
wire M1.power -> MO2.power
wire M1.power -> MO3.power

wire MO1.rotary -> GB1.in
wire GB1.out -> C1.drive

wire MO2.rotary -> GB2.in
wire GB2.out -> C2.drive
wire MO3.rotary -> GB3.in
wire GB3.out -> SC1.drive

wire I1.out -> C1.in
wire C1.out -> C2.in
wire C2.out -> SC1.in
wire SC1.out -> O1.solid
